  "interpretation": "How tightly an ensemble is wired to itself predicts how much it reactivates (Pearson r = 0.481, p = 0.0017, n = 40 ensemble-by-seed points). The comparison between the trained and untrained ensembles is therefore largely a comparison of their wiring, and cannot on its own establish that a memory drives reactivation. The test that holds wiring fixed and changes only the learned weights is trained versus unlearned."
